# @spectral/garden — species under @spectral family-root.
#
# The runtime name for a co-composing mesh of publishable-independent
# @systems (garden packages), each carrying its own author-attributed
# content-addressed identity, composing over the two-layer store/db
# split at runtime.
#
# Discharges the two-month forward-promise from `shards/spectral.mirror`
# (2026-05-25 → 2026-07-20) naming @spectral/garden as species landing
# at `shards/spectral/garden.mirror`. Sibling to @spectral/signature +
# @spectral/mosaic + @spectral/gen_prism + @spectral/supervisor +
# @spectral/portal + @spectral/entanglement + @spectral/registry +
# @spectral/root + @spectral/parent at the species altitude.
#
# Named 2026-07-20 by Alex Wolf, in-transcript, verbatim:
#   "I wanna build cosmos + spectral-db as the first garden packages
#    @~/dev/garden/{cosmos,spectral-db} (new folders)"
#
# The reification of cosmos + spectral-db as the first two garden
# packages is the second-witness that closes the mint gate. Prior
# first-witness territory:
#   - 2026-05-25 namespace insight naming @spectral/garden as species
#   - 2026-05-26 vetted-corpus insight extending the wine-cellar
#     metaphor (garden = cellar; vintner = curator; sommelier = peer)
#   - 2026-06-17 @spectral/garden/smarts as AGI at
#     substrate-architectural altitude
#   - 2026-06-24 @spectral/garden/git spec treating @spectral/garden
#     as forward-promised parent for /git sub-species
#
# === Canonical spec ===
#
# docs/specs/spectral-garden-cosmos-spectral-db-reification.md
# (Mara, 2026-07-20; Landing A). Grounds the reification of cosmos +
# spectral-db at `~/dev/garden/{cosmos,spectral-db}` as the first
# two garden packages.
#
# === Math foundation ===
#
# docs/math/2026-07-20-spectral-garden-mesh-of-systems.md
# (Mara, 2026-07-20; Landing B). Composes labeled directed graph
# theory + Grothendieck fibration + sheaf theory + Cauchy-
# completeness + Recognition #98 candidate second-witness territory
# at the mesh altitude.
#
# === What @spectral/garden IS ===
#
# A namespace-parent for the mesh-of-@systems living at
# `~/dev/garden/<package>/`. Each garden package is:
#
#   - Content-addressed at package altitude (garden-package-OID)
#   - Publishable-independent (own Cargo.toml, own flake.nix, own
#     git history, own release cadence)
#   - Substrate-composing at runtime (three composition altitudes:
#     `mirror.spec garden {}` block, `in @spectral/garden/<name>`
#     substrate-decl imports, `@io/git` + `@io/cargo` FLOOR crossings)
#   - Author-attributed by construction (via @spectral/signature
#     two-witness verification per gift-and-mirror-reflection §11.5)
#   - Per-package licensed (garden verifies signatures regardless
#     of license; license is a per-package curator decision per
#     2026-05-26 vetted-corpus insight §"business model honesty")
#
# The mesh is:
#
#   - Mesh-of-@systems, not legion-of-clones (heterogeneous tiles
#     fitted into coherent picture; each garden package is a distinct
#     shape composing with others)
#   - Autopoietic (grows by admitting new @systems as they mature;
#     existing packages content-addressed-permanent)
#   - Two-layer discipline preserved (open @mirror/store foundation
#     + closed-engine posture at @spectral/db altitude)
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Landing A §1 "Position" grounds the namespace-discipline choice
#   (species under @spectral, not family-root).
# - Landing B §5 surfaces Recognition #98 candidate second-witness
#   (garden-package-OID as fifth content-addressing altitude).
# - Landing B §7.4 grounds the Lagrange between narcissus-mesh
#   (monoculture) and splinter-mesh (fragmentation) at mesh altitude
#   per @autopoietic classifier-COORD.
# - #79 (Void-is-the-basis; @void.mirror 974a3f6): the mature garden
#   at garden.spectral.engineer is Cauchy-limit M_∞ per Landing B §4.3
#   — void-shaped ideal object.
# - #98 candidate (content-addressing cross-altitude composition):
#   this species-decl surfaces the fifth witness at garden-package-OID
#   altitude. Promotion is deferred to Alex tick.
#
# === Sibling / composition species ===
#
# Existing species under @spectral (peers at species altitude):
#   @spectral/signature   — rolling @song beat-chain (author attribution)
#   @spectral/mosaic      — heterogeneous-tiles cluster grammar
#   @spectral/gen_prism   — worker primitive
#   @spectral/supervisor  — lifecycle owner
#   @spectral/portal      — typed transport over content-addressed subspaces
#   @spectral/entanglement — sheaf restriction map at runtime altitude
#   @spectral/registry    — typed child index
#   @spectral/root        — parentless supervisor (the librarian's substrate type)
#   @spectral/parent      — single-parent acyclic lifecycle edge
#
# @spectral/garden composes with:
#   @spectral/signature — every garden package carries a signature
#                         beat-chain (two-witness author-attribution)
#   @mirror/store       — the open foundation garden packages layer over
#   @io/git             — garden packages are git-hosted per SEL-2.0
#
# Path-container discipline: this file at `shards/spectral/garden.mirror`
# declares `@spectral/garden` as species-under-@spectral. Sub-species
# land at `shards/spectral/garden/<name>.mirror` (e.g.,
# `shards/spectral/garden/cosmos.mirror`, `shards/spectral/garden/
# spectral-db.mirror`, `shards/spectral/garden/git.mirror` — per
# Landing A §7.3 Mara follow-up ticks).
#
# === Composition edges landed elsewhere ===
#
# - `shards/mirror/garden.mirror` — the CONSUMER-side substrate-decl
#   (the `garden { ~git'…' }` block shape in `mirror.spec`).
#   DIFFERENT altitude: @mirror/garden names the block-in-spec;
#   @spectral/garden names the runtime mesh those entries participate
#   in. Sibling altitudes, not siblings-in-hierarchy.
# - `docs/specs/spectral-garden-git-package-manager.md` (Mara,
#   2026-06-24) — @spectral/garden/git sub-species candidate. Landing
#   A §8 reconciliation: garden becomes species (this shard); /git
#   becomes sub-species under garden. Two-tier substrate-decl chain
#   is `@spectral (family-root) → @spectral/garden (this species) →
#   @spectral/garden/git (sub-species; forward-promised)`.
#
# === Marker-primary discipline ===
#
# Per @paradox.mirror precedent (1e17222; Mara 2026-07-20) + @void.mirror
# precedent (974a3f6; Reed 2026-07-18): the family/species declaration
# body is declarative-only. Bilaterals + actions are forward-promised
# at sub-species altitude where empirical firing has substrate-decl
# ground. This is Michelangelo-marble: land what the substrate is
# asking for (the species declaration + composition edges + docblock
# grounding); refuse abstractions the substrate hasn't asked for.
#
# The species IS the namespace-parent for the mesh; the mesh's
# operational surface (garden-membership verification, cross-package
# composition, mycelium routing) lives at sub-species altitude when
# empirical firings surface substrate demand.
#
# === Path-namespace property ===
#
# This file at `shards/spectral/garden.mirror` declares
# `@spectral/garden` per pact_matches_namespace (Seam Phase D
# efcef6e Cascade 1 enforcement).

prism @spectral/garden {
  focus  garden
  project garden
  split  garden
  shift  garden
  settle garden
}

out @spectral/garden
